From 54397cc832c3baa9b8c91a3c073915ed65334e73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:22:13 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add TMU traffic manager support

Add the TMU (Traffic Management Unit) layer. The TMU sits between
the CBM dequeue side and the switch: every egress port drains
through a TMU egress port, scheduler and queue, so even the minimal
"flat" datapath needs the TMU programmed.

drv_tmu_ll.c/h port the low-level table writers and the seven
sub-init routines (egress port map/occupancy/threshold/discard
tables, scheduler blocks, queue tables) as offset-based register
accesses, plus:

 - tmu_egress_port_enable(): enable one TMU egress port. Ordering
   matters at the consumer: the vendor enables the TMU egress port
   BEFORE opening the corresponding DMA dequeue channel, and this
   port follows that order in ndo_open.

 - tmu_create_flat_egress_path(): the minimal egress-port ->
   scheduler -> queue chain used for both the CPU dequeue ports
   (host RX) and the LAN TX dequeue port.

 - tmu_reset_mib_all() plus enqueue/dequeue counter resets and the
   QDCT walk zeroing per-queue state at init.

tmu_init.c sequences the whole block at CBM probe time.

Derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198),
tmu/drv_tmu_ll.c, tmu/drv_tmu_reg.h and include/net/drv_tmu_ll.h -
Copyright (c) 2012 Lantiq Deutschland GmbH; notices restored -
reduced to the minimum-viable subset this datapath exercises.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
